es": []}, {"definition": "(informal) Loosely, used to introduce a contrastive statement explaining why something wasn't successful, didn't happen, etc.", "tags": ["informal"], "examples": ["They fired tear gas at us, except the wind was blowing the wrong way.", "I almost walked out, except I remembered the promise I had made."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(archaic) Unless; used to introduce a hypothetical case in which an exception may exist.", "tags": ["archaic"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "And they sayde: We have no moo but five loves and two fisshes, except we shulde goo and bye meate for all this people.", "reference": "1526, [William Tyndale, transl.], The Newe Testamẽt […] (Tyndale Bible), [Worms, Germany: Peter Schöffer], →OCLC, Luke:"}, {"text": "If I ſay ſooth, I muſt report they were / As Cannons ouer-charg'd with double Cracks, / So they doubly redoubled ſtroakes vpon the Foe: / Except they meant to bathe in reeking Wounds, / Or memorize another Golgotha, / I cannot tell: but I am faint, / My Gaſhes cry for helpe.", "reference": "c. 1606 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedie of Macbeth”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act I, scene ii], page 131, column 2:"}, {"text": "Offensive wars, except the cause be very just, I will not allow of.", "reference": "1621, Robert Burton, The Anatomy of Melancholy, New York, published 2001, page 106:"}, {"text": "I am […] not so clear how you will be able to avoid it, except you assert the independence to which your estate gives you a title.", "reference": "1748, [Samuel Richardson], “Letter XXVII”, in Clarissa. Or, The History of a Young Lady: […], volume (please specify |volume=I to VII), London: […] S[amuel] Richardson; […], →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/except", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}